  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Addressing humanitarian, protection and health needs of Afghan undocumented returnees at the borders and in the provinces of high return andcontributing to emergency preparedness in Afghanistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The humanitarian situation in Afghanistan is characterized by structural and systemic challenges, including significant gender inequality, a constrained rights environment, inadequate essential services, a struggling economy, prolonged food insecurity, and frequent disasters related to natural hazards and climatic shocks. Through this project, IOM is addressing humanitarian protection and health needs of vulnerable returnees at the border with Iran and Pakistan and in the provinces of return through direct assistance that aims at reducing their vulnerability and increasing their capacity to address protection risks.</narrative>
  </description>
